{ "name":"tree_dnd_pointer_autoopen","component":"tree",
  "$comment":"openOnDropDelay. Hold a drag over a CLOSED folder and it opens under the cursor after 800ms, so a drop can reach somewhere that was not visible when the drag began. The `hold` on a dragpoint step is what makes it measurable at all: nothing shorter than the delay can observe it, and the two halves of a split hold have to add up rather than restart. `archive` is the only closed folder here, on purpose.",
